#X obj 673 11 math.abs~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 280 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Computes the absolute value of the input signal: negative
values become positive \, positive values stay unchanged. This is the
audio-rate equivalent of the [math.abs] object.;
#X text 240 153 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 178 • Rectifying a signal — converting a bipolar audio
signal into a unipolar one \, for example as a first step of an envelope
follower or a full-wave rectifier.;
#X text 250 233 • Extracting amplitude — measuring how far a signal
deviates from zero \, regardless of its sign \, for level detection
or modulation purposes.;
#X text 250 288 • Waveform transformation — turning a sine or triangle
wave into a "folded" waveform with a distinctive harmonic content \,
useful for creative waveshaping.;
